# A child's window title (OSC 0 / OSC 2) names its tab, as it does in
# every terminal's tab: zsh and bash prompts, vim, ssh and htop all set
# it, and with ten shells open it is what tells them apart. The user's
# own `:rename` outranks it; the label the pane opened with is the
# fallback.
command view.toggle_tree
ex term printf '\033]2;build-watch\007'; sleep 30
wait 1500
expect screen contains "build-watch"
expect pane build-watch
ex rename mine
expect screen contains "mine"
expect screen lacks "build-watch"
